      "message": "So this is an early design review, right? Maybe tag the cl with WIP?\n\nOne unhandled use case I see would be `it\u0027s_a_file_with_apostrophes\u0027.png`. I remember an AWCY dataset containing apostrophes and commas.\n\nI believe \"merging\" tokens during the `strtok()` loop would be clearer to understand rather than preemptively putting the next quoted string aside, tokenizing up to it, getting the stashed quoted string back, and repeating. Unfortunately `strtok()` uses an internal static state so this might not be doable. I guess implementing the whole parsing algorithm without using `strtok()` would be simpler to understand, but I think the current version with a fix for quotes in the middle of tokens would be the shortest.",
